{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "kjv-mark-004",
  "collection": "kjv-bible",
  "document_type": "bible_chapter",
  "number": 4,
  "title": "Mark 4",
  "display_title": "Mark 4",
  "translation": "King James Version",
  "translationCode": "KJV",
  "bookId": "mark",
  "book": "Mark",
  "bookName": "Mark",
  "bookOrder": 41,
  "testament": "new",
  "chapter": 4,
  "sortOrder": 41004,
  "verseCount": 41,
  "aliases": [
    "Mark",
    "Mrk",
    "Mk"
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:mark:4:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "And he began again to teach by the sea side: and there was gathered unto him a great multitude, so that he entered into a ship, and sat in the sea; and the whole multitude was by the sea on the land.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Mark 4:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:mark:4:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:mark:4:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "And he taught them many things by parables, and said unto them in his doctrine,",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Mark 4:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:mark:4:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:mark:4:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "Hearken; Behold, there went out a sower to sow:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Mark 4:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:mark:4:3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-004",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 4,
      "verseId": "kjv:mark:4:4",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "And it came to pass, as he sowed, some fell by the way side, and the fowls of the air came and devoured it up.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Mark 4:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:mark:4:4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-005",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 5,
      "verseId": "kjv:mark:4:5",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "And some fell on stony ground, where it had not much earth; and immediately it sprang up, because it had no depth of earth:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Mark 4:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:mark:4:5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-006",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 6,
      "verseId": "kjv:mark:4:6",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "But when the sun was up, it was scorched; and because it had no root, it withered away.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Mark 4:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:mark:4:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-007",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 7,
      "verseId": "kjv:mark:4:7",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "And some fell among thorns, and the thorns grew up, and choked it, and it yielded no fruit.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Mark 4:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:mark:4:7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-008",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 8,
      "verseId": "kjv:mark:4:8",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "And other fell on good ground, and did yield fruit that sprang up and increased; and brought forth, some thirty, and some sixty, and some an hundred.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Mark 4:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:mark:4:8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-009",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 9,
      "verseId": "kjv:mark:4:9",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "And he said unto them, He that hath ears to hear, let him hear.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Mark 4:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:mark:4:9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-010",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 10,
      "verseId": "kjv:mark:4:10",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "And when he was alone, they that were about him with the twelve asked of him the parable.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Mark 4:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:mark:4:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-011",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 11,
      "verseId": "kjv:mark:4:11",
      "numberLabel": "11",
      "text": "And he said unto them, Unto you it is given to know the mystery of the kingdom of God: but unto them that are without, all these things are done in parables:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Mark 4:11",
        "verseKey": "kjv:mark:4:11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-012",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 12,
      "verseId": "kjv:mark:4:12",
      "numberLabel": "12",
      "text": "That seeing they may see, and not perceive; and hearing they may hear, and not understand; lest at any time they should be converted, and their sins should be forgiven them.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Mark 4:12",
        "verseKey": "kjv:mark:4:12"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-013",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 13,
      "verseId": "kjv:mark:4:13",
      "numberLabel": "13",
      "text": "And he said unto them, Know ye not this parable? and how then will ye know all parables?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Mark 4:13",
        "verseKey": "kjv:mark:4:13"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-014",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 14,
      "verseId": "kjv:mark:4:14",
      "numberLabel": "14",
      "text": "The sower soweth the word.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Mark 4:14",
        "verseKey": "kjv:mark:4:14"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-015",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 15,
      "verseId": "kjv:mark:4:15",
      "numberLabel": "15",
      "text": "And these are they by the way side, where the word is sown; but when they have heard, Satan cometh immediately, and taketh away the word that was sown in their hearts.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Mark 4:15",
        "verseKey": "kjv:mark:4:15"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-016",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 16,
      "verseId": "kjv:mark:4:16",
      "numberLabel": "16",
      "text": "And these are they likewise which are sown on stony ground; who, when they have heard the word, immediately receive it with gladness;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Mark 4:16",
        "verseKey": "kjv:mark:4:16"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-017",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 17,
      "verseId": "kjv:mark:4:17",
      "numberLabel": "17",
      "text": "And have no root in themselves, and so endure but for a time: afterward, when affliction or persecution ariseth for the word’s sake, immediately they are offended.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Mark 4:17",
        "verseKey": "kjv:mark:4:17"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-018",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 18,
      "verseId": "kjv:mark:4:18",
      "numberLabel": "18",
      "text": "And these are they which are sown among thorns; such as hear the word,",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Mark 4:18",
        "verseKey": "kjv:mark:4:18"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-019",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 19,
      "verseId": "kjv:mark:4:19",
      "numberLabel": "19",
      "text": "And the cares of this world, and the deceitfulness of riches, and the lusts of other things entering in, choke the word, and it becometh unfruitful.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Mark 4:19",
        "verseKey": "kjv:mark:4:19"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-020",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 20,
      "verseId": "kjv:mark:4:20",
      "numberLabel": "20",
      "text": "And these are they which are sown on good ground; such as hear the word, and receive it, and bring forth fruit, some thirtyfold, some sixty, and some an hundred.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Mark 4:20",
        "verseKey": "kjv:mark:4:20"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-021",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 21,
      "verseId": "kjv:mark:4:21",
      "numberLabel": "21",
      "text": "And he said unto them, Is a candle brought to be put under a bushel, or under a bed? and not to be set on a candlestick?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Mark 4:21",
        "verseKey": "kjv:mark:4:21"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-022",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 22,
      "verseId": "kjv:mark:4:22",
      "numberLabel": "22",
      "text": "For there is nothing hid, which shall not be manifested; neither was any thing kept secret, but that it should come abroad.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Mark 4:22",
        "verseKey": "kjv:mark:4:22"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-023",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 23,
      "verseId": "kjv:mark:4:23",
      "numberLabel": "23",
      "text": "If any man have ears to hear, let him hear.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Mark 4:23",
        "verseKey": "kjv:mark:4:23"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-024",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 24,
      "verseId": "kjv:mark:4:24",
      "numberLabel": "24",
      "text": "And he said unto them, Take heed what ye hear: with what measure ye mete, it shall be measured to you: and unto you that hear shall more be given.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Mark 4:24",
        "verseKey": "kjv:mark:4:24"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-025",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 25,
      "verseId": "kjv:mark:4:25",
      "numberLabel": "25",
      "text": "For he that hath, to him shall be given: and he that hath not, from him shall be taken even that which he hath.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Mark 4:25",
        "verseKey": "kjv:mark:4:25"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-026",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 26,
      "verseId": "kjv:mark:4:26",
      "numberLabel": "26",
      "text": "And he said, So is the kingdom of God, as if a man should cast seed into the ground;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Mark 4:26",
        "verseKey": "kjv:mark:4:26"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-027",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 27,
      "verseId": "kjv:mark:4:27",
      "numberLabel": "27",
      "text": "And should sleep, and rise night and day, and the seed should spring and grow up, he knoweth not how.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Mark 4:27",
        "verseKey": "kjv:mark:4:27"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-028",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 28,
      "verseId": "kjv:mark:4:28",
      "numberLabel": "28",
      "text": "For the earth bringeth forth fruit of herself; first the blade, then the ear, after that the full corn in the ear.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Mark 4:28",
        "verseKey": "kjv:mark:4:28"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-029",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 29,
      "verseId": "kjv:mark:4:29",
      "numberLabel": "29",
      "text": "But when the fruit is brought forth, immediately he putteth in the sickle, because the harvest is come.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Mark 4:29",
        "verseKey": "kjv:mark:4:29"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-030",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 30,
      "verseId": "kjv:mark:4:30",
      "numberLabel": "30",
      "text": "And he said, Whereunto shall we liken the kingdom of God? or with what comparison shall we compare it?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Mark 4:30",
        "verseKey": "kjv:mark:4:30"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-031",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 31,
      "verseId": "kjv:mark:4:31",
      "numberLabel": "31",
      "text": "It is like a grain of mustard seed, which, when it is sown in the earth, is less than all the seeds that be in the earth:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Mark 4:31",
        "verseKey": "kjv:mark:4:31"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-032",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 32,
      "verseId": "kjv:mark:4:32",
      "numberLabel": "32",
      "text": "But when it is sown, it groweth up, and becometh greater than all herbs, and shooteth out great branches; so that the fowls of the air may lodge under the shadow of it.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Mark 4:32",
        "verseKey": "kjv:mark:4:32"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-033",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 33,
      "verseId": "kjv:mark:4:33",
      "numberLabel": "33",
      "text": "And with many such parables spake he the word unto them, as they were able to hear it.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Mark 4:33",
        "verseKey": "kjv:mark:4:33"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-034",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 34,
      "verseId": "kjv:mark:4:34",
      "numberLabel": "34",
      "text": "But without a parable spake he not unto them: and when they were alone, he expounded all things to his disciples.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Mark 4:34",
        "verseKey": "kjv:mark:4:34"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-035",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 35,
      "verseId": "kjv:mark:4:35",
      "numberLabel": "35",
      "text": "And the same day, when the even was come, he saith unto them, Let us pass over unto the other side.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Mark 4:35",
        "verseKey": "kjv:mark:4:35"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-036",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 36,
      "verseId": "kjv:mark:4:36",
      "numberLabel": "36",
      "text": "And when they had sent away the multitude, they took him even as he was in the ship. And there were also with him other little ships.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Mark 4:36",
        "verseKey": "kjv:mark:4:36"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-037",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 37,
      "verseId": "kjv:mark:4:37",
      "numberLabel": "37",
      "text": "And there arose a great storm of wind, and the waves beat into the ship, so that it was now full.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Mark 4:37",
        "verseKey": "kjv:mark:4:37"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-038",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 38,
      "verseId": "kjv:mark:4:38",
      "numberLabel": "38",
      "text": "And he was in the hinder part of the ship, asleep on a pillow: and they awake him, and say unto him, Master, carest thou not that we perish?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Mark 4:38",
        "verseKey": "kjv:mark:4:38"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-039",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 39,
      "verseId": "kjv:mark:4:39",
      "numberLabel": "39",
      "text": "And he arose, and rebuked the wind, and said unto the sea, Peace, be still. And the wind ceased, and there was a great calm.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Mark 4:39",
        "verseKey": "kjv:mark:4:39"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-040",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 40,
      "verseId": "kjv:mark:4:40",
      "numberLabel": "40",
      "text": "And he said unto them, Why are ye so fearful? how is it that ye have no faith?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Mark 4:40",
        "verseKey": "kjv:mark:4:40"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-041",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 41,
      "verseId": "kjv:mark:4:41",
      "numberLabel": "41",
      "text": "And they feared exceedingly, and said one to another, What manner of man is this, that even the wind and the sea obey him?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Mark 4:41",
        "verseKey": "kjv:mark:4:41"
      }
    }
  ],
  "source": {
    "repository": "aruljohn/Bible-kjv",
